			"notes": "### What's New in v2.1.0\n\n#### 1. Multi-Loader Server Adapters\n- Dedicated server mod artifacts for **Fabric**, **Forge**, and **NeoForge**.\n- Shares the proven core rule engine, multi-tier cache, and developer API with asynchronous login interception and Brigadier command registration.\n- Added candidate adapters for **Sponge**, **Geyser standalone**, and generic Java gateways.\n\n#### 2. Native Pumpkin WASI Component\n- Self-contained Rust/WASI plugin built specifically for Pumpkin servers.\n- Supports both Java and Bedrock admission with native country, ASN, and VPN policy enforcement, persistent caching, and native commands without requiring a Java bridge.\n\n#### 3. Local Connection Access Control\n- Opt-in \\\blockLocalConnections\\ and custom \\kickMessageLocalConnection\\ settings.\n- Rejects loopback (\\127.0.0.1\\), LAN, link-local, and IPv6 unique-local addresses before geolocation queries occur.\n- Country \\BLOCKLIST\\ with \\LOCAL\\ now also evaluates and blocks local player addresses with \\kickMessageCountry\\.\n- Auto-migrating configuration schema v6 ensures safe defaults without modifying existing custom settings.\n\n#### 4. Geyser & Floodgate Bedrock Integration\n- Deep integration with Geyser resolving trusted Bedrock client sockets and honoring configured Bedrock bypass rules.\n\n#### 5. Network & Fallback Hardening\n- Reject non-ASCII digits in IPv4 strings before Java resolution to avoid DNS leakage.\n- Strict expanded and mapped IPv6 normalization across Cloudflare Worker and VPS fallback gateway.\n- Modernized Docker container runtime on Node 22 LTS with automated healthcheck probes.\n\n---\n**Full Changelog**: https://github.com/DemonZ-Development/Geo-Restrict/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md"
		},
